{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_21","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"find /home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/17 -maxdepth 2 -type f | sort | xargs -r -n 1 sh -c 'echo \\\"=== \"'$1 ===\"; sed -n \"1,220p\" \"$1\"'\"' sh\"","aggregated_output":"=== /home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/17/des.md ===\n<new_puzzle>\n- `description`：根据边框缺口方向选择内部图案的旋转方式，再依据框内标记像素的颜色对旋转后的图案进行重新着色。\n- `Input structure`：\n  - 背景为黑色（black）。\n  - 网格中散布若干相同大小的正方形边框（由灰色 grey 像素绘制，边框宽度为一个像素）。\n  - 每个边框的四条边中恰好有一条边存在一个单像素宽的缺口（缺口位置为该边的中点处，缺口处像素为黑色背景色）。\n  - 每个边框内部（不含边框本身）包含一个由蓝色（blue）像素构成的小型非对称图案，该图案在所有边框中形状完全相同且未经旋转。\n  - 每个边框内部还包含恰好一个标记像素，该标记像素的颜色既不是黑色、也不是灰色、也不是蓝色，而是某种其他颜色（如 red、green、yellow 等）。该标记像素位于边框内部的某个空白位置。\n- `Rule`：\n  - 对于每个边框，首先判断缺口所在的边：上边缺口对应 0 度旋转（不旋转）、右边缺口对应顺时针 90 度旋转、下边缺口对应 180 度旋转、左边缺口对应顺时针 270 度旋转。\n  - 将边框内部的蓝色图案按上述角度进行旋转（以边框内部区域中心为旋转中心）。\n  - 旋转完成后，将图案中所有蓝色像素替换为该边框内标记像素的颜色。\n  - 标记像素本身在输出中被清除为黑色背景。\n  - 灰色边框和缺口保持不变。\n- `Key insight`：缺口方向编码旋转角度，框内彩色标记编码输出颜色——两个独立的隐含信息通道控制同一个图案的两种不同变换，解题者必须同时发现两条规则才能正确还原输出。\n</new_puzzle>\n\n<new_puzzle>\n- `description`：在网格中找到成对的同色 L 形标记，将每对 L 形所围成的矩形区域填充为该颜色，再根据矩形内预置的\"孔洞模板\"像素进行挖空。\n- `Input structure`：\n  - 背景为黑色（black）。\n  - 网格中散布若干对同色的 L 形标记（每个 L 形由三个像素组成：一个拐角像素和两个分别沿水平、垂直方向延伸一格的臂像素）。每种非黑颜色恰好出现两个 L 形。\n  - 同色的两个 L 形总是面朝相反方向（例如一个开口朝右下，另一个开口朝左上），它们共同界定一个矩形区域的两个对角。\n  - 在该矩形区域内部，可能存在若干白色（指 grey 灰色）像素，这些像素是\"孔洞模板\"。\n- `Rule`：\n  - 对于每对同色 L 形，确定它们的拐角像素所界定的矩形区域（以两个拐角像素为对角点的最小外接矩形）。\n  - 将该矩形区域内所有黑色像素填充为该 L 形的颜色。\n  - 矩形区域内原本为灰色（grey）的\"孔洞模板\"像素保持为黑色（即不填充），形成挖空效果。\n  - L 形标记本身保留在输出中。\n  - 不同颜色的矩形若发生重叠，后处理的颜色覆盖先处理的颜色（处理顺序按颜色在网格中首次出现的行优先、列其次排序）。\n- `Key insight`：两个反向 L 形不是装饰图案，而是矩形对角的指示器——解题者需要先识别出\"成对反向 L 形 = 矩形端点\"这一空间编码，然后还需发现灰色像素是挖空模板而非填充内容，两层规则缺一不可。\n</new_puzzle>\n\n<new_puzzle>\n- `description`：将散落的彩色碎片按形状匹配嵌入灰色模板的对应凹槽中，碎片的朝向由凹槽的朝向决定。\n- `Input structure`：\n  - 背景为黑色（black）。\n  - 网格中有一个大型灰色（grey）连通区域作为\"模板\"，模板整体近似矩形，但边缘有若干凹槽（凹槽是从模板边缘向内凹进的缺失区域，形状各异，每个凹槽恰好可容纳一个碎片）。\n  - 在模板外部散布若干彩色碎片（每个碎片是一个 4-连通的单色对象，颜色各不相同，如 red、blue、green、yellow 等）。\n  - 每个碎片的像素数量与恰好一个凹槽的像素数量相同，且碎片经过 0/90/180/270 度旋转后形状与该凹槽完全吻合。\n  - 碎片数量等于凹槽数量，一一对应且无歧义。\n- `Rule`：\n  - 对于每个凹槽，在所有碎片中找到形状匹配的那个碎片（可能需要旋转 0/90/180/270 度中的某一个角度才能吻合）。\n  - 将该碎片以匹配的旋转角度放入凹槽的位置，碎片像素保持其原本颜色。\n  - 碎片原来所在的位置被清除为黑色背景。\n  - 灰色模板本身保持不变。\n- `Key insight`：解题者需要同时完成两步非平凡推理——第一步是通过形状匹配（含旋转）找到碎片与凹槽的配对关系，第二步是确定正确的旋转角度使碎片恰好嵌入凹槽。碎片的颜色仅用于区分不同碎片，不参与匹配逻辑。\n</new_puzzle>\n\n<new_puzzle>\n- `description`：利用网格边缘的颜色序列条作为\"绘图指令\"，在中央画布上逐步绘制嵌套的彩色矩形环。\n- `Input structure`：\n  - 背景为黑色（black）。\n  - 网格的最左列是一个自上而下排列的颜色序列条，由若干种不同颜色的像素组成（每种颜色占连续若干个像素）。该列中不含黑色像素。\n  - 网格的最上行（不含第一列的交叉像素）是另一个自左而右排列的颜色序列条，同样由若干种不同颜色的像素组成，每种颜色占连续若干个像素，不含黑色。\n  - 网格其余区域（不含最左列和最上行）为全黑的\"画布\"区域。\n  - 最左列中每段连续同色像素的长度记录了对应矩形环在垂直方向上的厚度；最上行中每段连续同色像素的长度记录了对应矩形环在水平方向上的厚度。\n  - 最左列与最上行的颜色段数量相同，且颜色按顺序一一对应（第一段对应第一段，依此类推），定义同一个矩形环的颜色。\n- `Rule`：\n  - 从最外层开始，依次绘制嵌套矩形环：第一个颜色段定义最外层环，第二个颜色段定义次外层环，依此类推。\n  - 每个矩形环的上下厚度等于最左列对应颜色段的像素数，左右厚度等于最上行对应颜色段的像素数。\n  - 矩形环从画布区域的外边界开始向内嵌套绘制：第一个环紧贴画布边界，第二个环紧贴第一个环的内边界，以此类推。\n  - 每个环的颜色为对应颜色段的颜色。\n  - 最左列和最上行在输出中保持不变。\n- `Key insight`：边缘的两个颜色序列条不是简单的图例，而是分别编码了矩形环在两个维度上的厚度——解题者需要发现\"颜色段长度 = 环厚度\"这一数值编码关系，并且需要理解两条序列如何协同定义非正方形的矩形环。\n</new_puzzle>\n\n<new_puzzle>\n- `description`：根据种子像素的颜色从色板区域选取对应的小图案，再按种子像素相对于分隔线的位置决定图案的镜像翻转方式，最后将图案印在种子像素所在位置。\n- `Input structure`：\n  - 背景为黑色（black）。\n  - 网格被一条红色（red）水平线和一条红色垂直线分成四个象限。两条线各为一个像素宽，交叉于网格中部。\n  - 左上象限是\"色板区域\"：其中包含若干个小型彩色图案（每个图案是一个 4-连通的单色对象），每个图案的颜色各不相同。每个图案的尺寸不超过 3x3。\n  - 其余三个象限（右上、左下、右下）是\"画布区域\"：其中散布若干单个彩色像素作为\"种子像素\"，每个种子像素的颜色与色板区域中某个图案的颜色相同。\n- `Rule`：\n  - 对于每个种子像素，根据其颜色在色板区域找到对应的图案。\n  - 根据种子像素所在的象限决定图案的翻转方式：右上象限的种子使用水平镜像翻转（左右翻转），左下象限的种子使用垂直镜像翻转（上下翻转），右下象限的种子同时进行水平和垂直翻转（等效于 180 度旋转）。\n  - 将翻转后的图案以种子像素为锚点绘制到画布上。锚点对应图案在色板区域中的左上角像素的相对位置。\n  - 种子像素本身被图案覆盖。色板区域和红色分隔线保持不变。\n- `Key insight`：色板区域提供形状模板，种子颜色提供匹配键，而种子所在象限提供翻转指令——三个独立的信息来源（形状、颜色匹配、空间位置）分别控制变换的不同方面。解题者必须同时发现象限与翻转类型的映射关系以及颜色与图案的匹配关系。\n</new_puzzle>\n\n<new_puzzle>\n- `description`：识别网格中的\"信号塔\"和\"接收器\"，沿信号塔的天线方向发射射线，射线长度由信号塔底座的像素数决定，射线到达接收器后将接收器重新着色。\n- `Input structure`：\n  - 背景为黑色（black）。\n  - 网格中有若干\"信号塔\"对象，每个信号塔由两部分组成：一个水平或垂直的单像素宽的\"底座\"（由灰色 grey 像素构成，长度为 2 至 6 个像素），以及从底座的某一端垂直延伸出的单个彩色像素作为\"天线\"（天线颜色各不相同，如 red、blue、green 等）。天线总是从底座端点向外延伸一格。\n  - 网格中还有若干\"接收器\"，每个接收器是一个单独的灰色（grey）像素，不与任何信号塔相邻。\n  - 天线像素延伸的方向即为信号发射方向（从底座端点经过天线继续向外延伸的方向）。\n- `Rule`：\n  - 对于每个信号塔，从天线像素出发，沿天线方向（即从底座指向天线的方向继续延伸）绘制一条射线。射线长度等于该信号塔底座的灰色像素数量（不含天线本身）。射线颜色与天线颜色相同。\n  - 如果射线的末端像素恰好落在某个灰色接收器上，或射线路径经过某个灰色接收器，则将该接收器像素重新着色为天线的颜色。\n  - 射线路径上的非接收器黑色像素也被着色为天线颜色（即射线可见）。\n  - 如果射线路径被非黑色、非灰色像素阻挡，射线在阻挡处停止。\n  - 信号塔本身（底座和天线）保持不变。\n- `Key insight`：底座不仅是视觉上的支撑结构，其长度还编码了射线的传播距离——解题者需要先识别出\"底座长度 = 射线长度\"这一数值关系，再结合天线方向确定射线的路径和终点。接收器的变色则是验证射线是否\"到达\"的视觉反馈。\n</new_puzzle>\n\n<new_puzzle>\n- `description`：在包含多个彩色区域的网格中，每个区域的边界像素根据其相邻区域的颜色进行混合重绘，而区域内部保持原色不变。\n- `Input structure`：\n  - 网格被若干单像素宽的黑色（black）分隔线划分成若干矩形区域（类似格子窗）。\n  - 每个矩形区域内部填充单一颜色（非黑色），不同区域可以有不同颜色，也可以有相同颜色。\n  - 黑色分隔线形成规则的行列网格结构。\n  - 网格的最外圈边框也是黑色。\n- `Rule`：\n  - 黑色分隔线在输出中保持不变。\n  - 对于每个矩形区域，检查其四个方向（上、下、左、右）相邻的矩形区域（隔一条黑色分隔线的邻居）。\n  - 如果某个区域的所有相邻区域（存在的方向）颜色全部相同，则该区域被重绘为邻居的颜色。\n  - 如果某个区域的相邻区域颜色不全相同（至少有两个邻居颜色不同），则该区域保持原色不变。\n  - 位于网格边缘的区域，不存在的方向不计入判断（即只看存在的邻居）。\n- `Key insight`：表面上看是一个颜色扩散问题，但实际规则是\"共识覆盖\"——只有当所有邻居\"意见一致\"时才改变自身颜色。解题者需要从多个样例中排除简单的多数投票、最近邻扩散等假设，发现\"全一致才变色\"这一严格条件。\n</new_puzzle>\n\n<new_puzzle>\n- `description`：将网格中的每个多色复合对象拆解为单色层，按各层面积从大到小依次垂直堆叠到输出网格的指定列中。\n- `Input structure`：\n  - 背景为黑色（black）。\n  - 网格中有若干个空间上分离的\"复合对象\"。每个复合对象是一个 8-连通的多色区域，内部包含 2 到 4 种不同的非黑颜色，每种颜色构成一个 4-连通的单色子层。\n  - 网格底部有一行灰色（grey）像素构成的\"基准线\"，基准线上方是对象区域。\n  - 基准线上每个复合对象的正下方恰好有一个与该对象中某种颜色相同的\"锚点标记\"像素（位于基准线上）。\n- `Rule`：\n  - 对于每个复合对象，将其拆解为各单色子层，并分别计算每个子层的像素数量（面积）。\n  - 在输出网格中，以基准线上锚点标记所在的列为中心列。\n  - 将各子层按面积从大到小、从基准线向上依次堆叠：面积最大的子层紧贴基准线上方，次大的在其上方，依此类推。\n  - 每个子层在输出中表示为一个水平色条，宽度为 1 列（即锚点所在列），高度等于该子层的面积（像素数）。色条颜色为该子层的颜色。\n  - 复合对象原来所在的位置被清除为黑色。基准线保持不变。\n- `Key insight`：复合对象不是按空间位置重排，而是被\"分析\"为颜色层并按面积排序后重新编码为一维柱状图——解题者需要先发现拆层和面积计数的操作，再发现堆叠顺序的排序规则，最后理解锚点标记确定输出位置这三层逻辑。\n</new_puzzle>\n=== /home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/17/ids.txt ===\neval/58490d8a\ntrain/17b866bd\ntrain/e3f79277\neval/e3721c99\ntrain/34cfa167\ntrain/985ae207\ntrain/abbfd121\ntrain/5adee1b2\neval/65b59efc\neval/f931b4a8\ntrain/ac0c2ac3\neval/4c3d4a41\ntrain/182e5d0f\ntrain/9caf5b84\neval/8e5c0c38\ntrain/f0100645\neval/7ed72f31\ntrain/1b59e163\ntrain/ad38a9d0\ntrain/fd02da9e\n=== /home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/17/prompt.md ===\n你是一个 ARC-AGI 谜题设计专家。下面的 20 道参考题是难度和机制质量的标杆。仔细阅读每道题的**解题逻辑**（解题者从样例归纳规则的认知过程），而非表面场景。你的新题应在机制深度和隐蔽性上与参考题持平或者实现超越。\n\n每个参考题描述包含：\n- `description`：一句话概述题目的变换目标。\n- `Input structure`：输入网格中有哪些对象、背景、标记、边界或组件。\n- `Rule`：从输入到输出的确定性变换规则。\n- `Key insight`：解题所需的核心洞见。\n\n参考题目如下：\n<reference_puzzle index=\"1\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"58490d8a\" lines=\"9-21\">\n<description>\nCount colored objects and record tallies inside a legend box.\n\nInput structure:\n- A black rectangular legend box with key-color pixels in its leftmost non-black column.\n- Outside the box, distinct objects of each key color are scattered across the grid.\n\nRule:\n- For each key color, count separate same-colored objects outside the legend box.\n- Output the legend box repainted: each key row gets one dot per object, spaced every other cell rightward from the key pixel.\n\nKey insight: The legend is both the color index and the output canvas — object counts become dot sequences on the matching row.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"2\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"17b866bd\" lines=\"49-67\">\n<description>\nMove each marker from a lattice corner gap into the adjacent enclosed 12-pixel cavity.\n\nInput structure:\n- The grid is a repeated teal lattice around black 12-pixel cavities.\n- A marker is a non-black pixel placed at the northwest corner gap of one\n  complete 5x5 lattice tile; the marker may itself be teal.\n\nRule:\n- For every marked northwest corner gap, clear that marker to black.\n- Fill the 12 black pixels in the tile immediately down-right of the marker\n  with the marker color.\n- Leave the rest of the lattice unchanged.\n\nKey insight:\n- The apparent isolated markers are control pixels for the adjacent cavity;\n  teal markers are recognized as extra teal pixels occupying a gap that the\n  periodic lattice template says should be black.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"3\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"e3f79277\" lines=\"8-23\">\n<description>\nReplace a corner L with a same-color right-triangle outline in the corresponding corner of an enlarged canvas.\n\nInput structure:\n- The input is a square grid with one background color and one foreground color.\n- The foreground is a one-pixel-thick L inside a square bbox.\n- The L touches exactly one horizontal grid edge and one vertical grid edge, identifying a corner.\n\nRule:\n- Fill a square output canvas of side 3n-2, where n is the input side length, with the background color.\n- Double the L leg length to get the triangle side length.\n- Draw the two perpendicular triangle legs on the same output corner edges and connect their free endpoints with the diagonal.\n\nKey insight:\n- The input L encodes the corner, color, and side length of the triangle outline; the missing side is the diagonal between the L's two free endpoints.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"4\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"e3721c99\" lines=\"69-83\">\n<description>\nRecolor grey shapes by matching their hole count to a color legend.\n\nInput structure:\n- bg = most common color; grey (5) sprites scattered across the grid.\n- Colored legend shapes (non-bg, non-grey, at least 2×2, not touching the outer border) near grid edge,\n  each with a distinct number of enclosed holes.\n\nRule:\n- Each colored legend shape defines a mapping: hole count → color.\n- For every grey sprite, count its holes (enclosed bg regions not touching the sprite's bounding-box border).\n- Recolor the grey sprite to the matching legend color; erase grey distractors with unlisted hole counts.\n\nKey insight: Shape identity is encoded by topology (number of holes), not geometry or size.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"5\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"34cfa167\" lines=\"94-117\">\n<description>\nComplete a four-corner framed rectangle from one decorated anchor rectangle and its diagonal mate.\n\nInput structure:\n- The background is the dominant color.\n- Two same-color solid rectangular anchors of the same size sit on opposite\n  diagonal corners, with the first anchor above-left of the second.\n- The upper-left anchor has two one-cell-thick vertical control bars to its\n  right and two one-cell-thick horizontal control bars below it.\n\nRule:\n- Copy the anchor rectangle into the two missing corners of the implied\n  larger rectangle.\n- Repeat the right-side control bars horizontally between the left and right\n  anchors, using their spacing as the period, and draw the outer top and\n  bottom borders in the first right-control color.\n- Repeat the below-side control bars vertically between the top and bottom\n  anchors, using the same period, and draw the outer left and right borders\n  in the first below-control color.\n\nKey insight: The small control bars are the first two ticks of two periodic\nframe patterns; the diagonal anchor supplies the opposite corner and the\nmissing two anchor copies.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"6\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"985ae207\" lines=\"82-97\">\n<description>\nRepeat each 3x3 control-center sprite toward the matching solid rectangle until a copy first overlaps that rectangle.\n\nInput structure\n- The background is the dominant color.\n- Each sprite is a 3x3 foreground object whose eight border pixels have one color and whose center has a different control color.\n- For every control color, there is exactly one separate solid rectangular object of that color.\n\nRule\n- Match each sprite to the unique solid rectangle whose color equals the sprite center.\n- Copy the whole 3x3 sprite in the cardinal direction of that rectangle, stepping by three cells each time.\n- Stop after pasting the first copy whose 3x3 bbox overlaps the rectangle; copied pixels overwrite the rectangle there.\n\nKey insight\nThe center pixel is not the paint color: it is a destination key, while the entire 3x3 sprite is the motif tiled along the straight path.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"7\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"abbfd121\" lines=\"56-74\">\n<description>\nRecover the repeating background pattern hidden under the largest solid rectangle.\n\nInput structure:\n- The grid is covered by a small row/column periodic pattern.\n- Several non-pattern colors form solid rectangular foreground objects that\n  overwrite the pattern.\n- The requested output region is the largest of those solid rectangles.\n\nRule:\n- Find every 4-connected monochromatic object whose bounding box is a filled\n  rectangle with both dimensions greater than one.\n- Treat those rectangles as masks, infer the smallest repeating tile that is\n  consistent with all remaining visible pixels, and repaint the largest\n  rectangle's coordinates with that tile.\n\nKey insight: The rectangle colors are occluders; the visible pixels outside\nthem are enough to reconstruct the original periodic background underneath.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"8\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"5adee1b2\" lines=\"8-23\">\n<description>\nUse the left-edge color legend to draw a padded rectangular halo around each matching object while preserving enclosed holes.\n\nInput structure:\n- The grid has a dominant background color.\n- One or more two-row markers sit on the left edge; each marker is a 2x2 block whose left column is an object color and right column is its halo color.\n- Away from the markers, every source color from the legend appears as one or more 4-connected monochrome objects.\n\nRule:\n- Keep the input pixels unchanged.\n- For each source-color object, take its tight bbox expanded by one cell and clipped to the grid.\n- Recolor background pixels in that expanded region to the marker's halo color, except for background holes enclosed by the object.\n\nKey insight:\n- The small left-edge bars are a legend: they map object colors to the colors used for the surrounding padded bbox.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"9\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"65b59efc\" lines=\"9-24\">\n<description>\nDecode a stamp map: read templates, markers, and palette from a tiled grid, then render stamps.\n\nInput structure:\n- Grid divided into K tile columns (each N wide) separated by 1-col dashed separators.\n- Top band (rows 0..N-1): K template masks, one per tile column.\n- Middle band (rows N+1..2N): marker pixels whose color picks a template.\n- Bottom band (rows 2N+2..): K palette swatches giving the output color per template.\n- Separator rows at rows N and 2N+1 (dashed pattern of sep color).\n\nRule:\n- Each marker's local position (lr, lc) within its tile column determines which N×N output block to stamp.\n- The marker's color identifies which template to use; the palette recolors the template.\n\nKey insight: Marker color encodes template index; local position within tile column encodes stamp block.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"10\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"f931b4a8\" lines=\"10-27\">\n<description>\nCount the two upper quadrant control regions to size an output made from the lower quadrant pattern.\n\nInput structure:\n- The grid is an even square split into four equal quadrants.\n- Black is the background.\n- The upper-left and upper-right quadrants are control regions.\n- The lower-left quadrant is a color source tile; the lower-right quadrant is either a stencil tile or empty.\n\nRule:\n- Output height is the number of non-background pixels in the upper-left quadrant.\n- Output width is the number of non-background pixels in the upper-right quadrant.\n- If the lower-right stencil has foreground pixels, tile it over the output; each stencil background pixel is filled from the lower-left quadrant cell at the corresponding coarse tile position.\n- If the lower-right stencil is empty, tile the lower-left quadrant directly over the output.\n\nKey insight:\n- The top quadrants specify only dimensions, while the bottom quadrants specify a two-level repeated pattern: a fine stencil and coarse fill colors.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"11\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"ac0c2ac3\" lines=\"7-19\">\n<description>\nFill each centered square ring with the color of the marker at that ring distance.\n\nInput structure\nThe input is an odd square grid with a dominant background color and one\nnon-background marker for every Chebyshev distance from the grid center.\nRule\nThe output replaces the background with concentric square rings centered on\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
